==Icelandic==
===Noun===
'''elska''' {{f}} 

# [[affection]], [[love]]
#: ''Ekki gráta '''elsku''' vinur.''
#:: Don't cry '''dear''' friend.

====Declension====
{{Icelandic declension kvk vb 01 og 01a|elsk}}

====Derived terms====
*[[elskan mín]] (my love, [[dear]])

[[Category:Icelandic nouns]]

===Verb===
'''elska''' (+ {{accusative}}) ([[elskaði]])

# to [[love]]
#: ''Ég '''elska''' konuna mína.''
#:: I '''love''' my wife.
#: ''Hann '''elskaði''' mig aldrei.''
#:: He never '''loved''' me.

====Inflection====
{{Icelandic conjugation 01 vb -aði|elsk}}
 
====Usage notes====
* The verb '''elska''' is mostly used about people and animals or pets (though rarely). Almost never used about inanimate things such as pizza, cars etc.

===Derived terms===
* [[ég elska þig]] - I love you
* [[elska fram úr hófi]]
* [[elskast]]

